OL,3,AActor targets 'scarred villain' screen
OL,4,Astereotype
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn actor is backing a charity's call
OL,7,Ffor more positive roles for performers
OL,8,Fwith scars and visible differences.
OL,10,FNorthamptonshire-based Robert Rhodes,
OL,11,Fwho has appeared in Silent Witness and
OL,12,FHouse of the Dragon, said: "The media
OL,13,Findustry needs to start reflecting the
OL,14,Ftrue experience of people with visible
OL,15,Fdifference."
OL,17,FThe charity Changing Faces wants the
OL,18,Ffilm and TV industry to stop using
OL,19,Fscars, burns and other visible
OL,20,Fdifferences as marks of villainy and
OL,21,Fhas started a petition calling for more
OL,22,Fpositive representation.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,168,160,200,105,0,100
